PSI Access  is included with DECnet/OSI. There is a QIO interface to the X.29
stuff. The problem you have is finding the gateway box that the PSI Access
talks to. PSI Access talks Gateway Access Protocol over your LAN to this box
(we use X25 Router 2000 on DEMSB - unsupported for a long time but works).
The problem currently is buying a supported box that will act as a X.25 
gateway for PSI Access. Last time I looked the only one was an expensive
DECnis configuration. You can use a VAX as the gateway box if it has the
right sync comms cards (using DECnet/OSI + WANDD - I think you need a 
DVNETEXT licence for this). This may work on an Alpha too.

